{"type":"message","id":"4b01a71f","parentId":"bed5665e","timestamp":"2026-05-23T17:45:13.026Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Both threads only contain heartbeat messages from the agent itself (all start with \"**[Heartbeat\" and have \"threadId\" fields indicating they're the agent's own messages). There are no human discussions or other agent messages to respond to. The latest messages are around 23:50 UTC on both threads.\n\nCurrent time is 17:45 UTC on May 23rd, 2026. The heartbeats show timestamps around 1778975xxx which are much higher - those appear to be Unix timestamps in milliseconds. Let me check: 1778975520833 ms = 1778975520.833 seconds = about May 22, 2026. But wait, the heartbeat says \"23:50 UTC\" - but the current time is 17:45 UTC May 23rd. There's a discrepancy.\n\nActually looking at the timestamps more carefully:\n- msg_1778975520833 = Heartbeat 23:50 UTC\n- msg_1778975602235 = Heartbeat 23:50 UTC\n\nThese are Unix timestamps in milliseconds. 1778975520 seconds = May 22, 2026 roughly. But the heartbeat content says \"23:50 UTC\" - so maybe the timestamps in the messages are just IDs, not actual time.\n\nRegardless - both threads show only heartbeat messages from the agent itself. No human discussions, no new content to respond to.\n\nSince there's no human content to respond to, I should just send a heartbeat to both threads acknowledging the check and noting the status.","thinkingSignature":"9361dea76f894fc4bfe66623ea9467d7d4e1066fd05288a76848354a6cdc0016"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\n双线程均只有Heartbeat自动消息，无新增人类讨论。继续发送Heartbeat状态同步：\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_8im3z08ctgz5_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"curl -s -X POST \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/send\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -H \"X-API-Key: echo-a…-key\" \\\n  -d '{\n    \"threadId\": \"arbitration\",\n    \"content\": \"**[Heartbeat 17:45 UTC | 17:45检查 | 双线程无新增人类讨论 | 系统运行正常]**\\n